.SH "NAME"
aerospace-list-monitors \- Print monitors that satisfy conditions
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
aerospace list\-monitors [\-h|\-\-help] [\-\-focused [no]] [\-\-mouse [no]] [\-\-format <output\-format>] [\-\-count] [\-\-json]
.fi
.br
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Print monitors that satisfy conditions
.SH "OPTIONS"
.sp
\-h, \-\-help
.RS 4
Print help
.RE
.sp
\-\-focused [no]
.RS 4
Filter results to only print the focused monitor.
\f(CR[no]\fP inverts the condition
.RE
.sp
\-\-mouse [no]
.RS 4
Filter results to only print the monitor with the mouse.
\f(CR[no]\fP inverts the condition
.RE
.sp
\-\-format <output\-format>
.RS 4
Specify output format.
See "Output Format" section for more details.
Incompatible with \f(CR\-\-count\fP
.RE
.sp
\-\-count
.RS 4
Output only the number of monitors.
Incompatible with \f(CR\-\-format\fP
.RE
.sp
\-\-json
.RS 4
Output in JSON format.
Can be used in combination with \f(CR\-\-format\fP to specify which data to include into the json.
Incompatible with \f(CR\-\-count\fP
.RE
.SH "OUTPUT FORMAT"
.sp
Output format can be configured with optional \f(CR[\-\-format <output\-format>]\fP option.
\f(CR<output\-format>\fP supports \c
.URL "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/String_interpolation" "string interpolation" "."
.sp
If not specified, the default \f(CR<output\-format>\fP is:
.br
\f(CR%{monitor\-id}%{right\-padding} | %{monitor\-name}\fP
.sp
The following variables can be used inside \f(CR<output\-format>\fP:
.sp
%{monitor\-id}
.RS 4
1\-based Number. Sequential number of the belonging monitor
.RE
.sp
%{monitor\-appkit\-nsscreen\-screens\-id}
.RS 4
1\-based index of the belonging monitor in \f(CRNSScreen.screens\fP array. Useful for integration with other tools that might be using \f(CRNSScreen.screens\fP ordering (like sketchybar).
.RE
.sp
%{monitor\-name}
.RS 4
String. Name of the belonging monitor
.RE
.sp
%{monitor\-is\-main}
.RS 4
Boolean. True if the monitor is main.
.RE
.sp
%{right\-padding}
.RS 4
A special variable which expands with a minimum number of spaces required to form a right padding in the appropriate column
.RE
.sp
%{newline}
.RS 4
Unicode U+000A newline symbol \f(CR\(rsn\fP
.RE
.sp
%{tab}
.RS 4
Unicode U+0009 tab symbol \f(CR\(rst\fP
.RE
